# Explicit negation (docs/adr/0009, Q4): a claim may state that its proposition did not hold, over its own
# valid time. Only negations carry the attribute; a claim without it is positive, so existing claims, their
# ids and their proposition keys are unchanged. Additive only: rolling back means restoring the
# pre-migration export (docs/adr/0004), which is safe only while no negated claim has been recorded.

define
  attribute polarity, value string @values("negative");
  claim owns polarity;
